title: The Blood Atonement
description: Only the blood of Christ atones for sin: one offering, once for all, for the sins of the whole world, from the teachings on salvation.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-salvation-blood-atonement.html
highlight: blood

# Built from the teachings under "The blood atonement" in studies/data/topics/salvation.json,
# with standalone teachings on the same theme. Slide text is the author's own sentences.

=== Only the blood
# from 12415
--- The Blood Atonement [title]
overline: Doctrine · Salvation
heading: The Blood Atonement
sub: There is always a price for redemption. And the price for righteousness is Christ.
refs: Romans 3:25; Hebrews 9:22; Colossians 1:14
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 16360
--- The only propitiation
kicker: The doctrine
lead: Only the blood of a holy God offered in our place and sprinkled on the mercy seat can atone for our sin and justify us before God.
big: Romans 3:25 | mark: a propitiation through faith in his blood
p: That is the only propitiation. The blood is for the heavenly Father.

# from 16360
--- None of these things
panel-warn: None of these | Turning your life around, repenting of sin, joining a church, getting water baptized, making Jesus the Lord of your life, seeing real change, sacraments and good deeds… None of these things satisfy the price of sin.
rev: By his own blood | Hebrews 9:12

# from 8660
--- Christ offered once
lead: Substitutionary atonement, also called vicarious atonement, the Biblical understanding Jesus Christ being the sacrifice that takes away the sins of the whole world, to the salvation of those who believe.
scripture: Hebrews 9:26-28 | mark: once in the end of the world hath he appeared to put away sin by the sacrifice of himself
p: So Christ was offered once to bear our sins. And those of us who believed look to His coming to our day of redemption.

=== Pictures and the true
# from 8660, 8690, 17226
--- The blood of bulls and goats
big: Hebrews 10:4
p: Man has always been saved by grace through faith in Christ. The blood of bulls and goats never took away sins. It was not possible, the Bible says.
p: These sacrifices were for a time and a place and acted as a picture for the perfect sacrifice of Jesus Christ, Whose blood marked the promise of a better testament.
callout: Animal sacrifice never was a dispensation or ministration of salvation or grace or a means of justification.

# from 8660, 16360
--- The death of the testator
scripture: Hebrews 9:15-17 | mark: For where a testament is, there must also of necessity be the death of the testator
p: Jesus as the sole mediator between God and man was by the means of His death, becoming sin for the redemption of transgressions. (For sin is the transgression of the law).
p: A testament having no power while the testator liveth. And so the death of the testator signified that those called had come into their promised inheritance. Amen.

# from 8690
--- One offering perfected for ever
big: Hebrews 10:14
p: A better sacrifice, done once and forever. Taking on the sins of the whole world.
p: Practical application of this, the implications of this, that we are forgiven of all sin by this perfect sanctification, total remission, forever, is that we be freed from the burden of guilt and the fear of judgment that we may serve the living God.
refs: Hebrews 10:17-18

# from 8690
--- The conscience
lead: A conscience offended by sin, knowingly transgressing the law, with understanding, can only be made clean with the blood of Christ.
tile: Unsaved | Guilty
tile: Saved | Cleansed by the blood
tile: Reprobate | Seared by God for our hardened heart
p: These are the three spiritual states of man. Unsaved, saved and reprobate. And the underlying condition of fallen man comes in our conscience.
refs: Hebrews 9:14; Hebrews 10:22; 1 Timothy 4:2

=== The Son made flesh
# from 8503
--- A little lower than the angels
big: Hebrews 2:9
p: That the Creator became as the created that he may bring us to glory. That He, as the captain of our salvation was made perfect, complete, by the suffering of the cross and death as a sin offering.
p: Liberated from the fear of death found in transgression of the law by our redemption in His perfect work.
refs: Hebrews 2:14-15

# from 9782
--- He who knew no sin
lead: Jesus, as the burnt offering, the Holocaust, the propitiation of our sins that we may be justified in Him.
p: Many Christians gladly celebrate Easter, rejoicing that He is risen. Some will consider the pain and suffering of the cross. Few want to reflect on His torment in Hell for our sins. He who knew no sin, paying the price for us.
note: It’s something we should reflect on. [[2 Corinthians 5:21]]

=== Reconciled by His blood
# from 10791
--- While we were yet sinners
big: Romans 5:8
p: That when we were still enemies, working iniquities, dead in sin, God reconciled us through the death of His Son. God loved His enemies, and offered the free gift of salvation by the shedding of blood of His only begotten Son.
p: Think about this, for in it is the righteousness of God.
refs: Romans 5:9-11

# from 10790
--- Peace with God
big: Romans 5:1
p: The peace and goodwill on earth was come from God to man. Not the peace of men not warring. Not goodwill between tribes. But the enmity of wrath in the transgressions of man made justified by the peace offering of His only begotten Son.
callout: Note, “wherein we stand.” This isn’t the future, this isn’t a process. [[Romans 5:2]]

# from 14934
--- Redemption through His blood
scripture: Colossians 1:12-14 | mark: In whom we have redemption through his blood, even the forgiveness of sins
p: We are now reconciled, having made peace with the Father through the blood of the Son.
p: This is the good news, the glory of the Gospel of God. All of these promises have been fulfilled already, the moment you believed.
refs: Colossians 1:20-21

# from 6854
--- For the whole world
big: 1 John 2:2
p: We need Christ to be the sacrifice, the sole propitiation for our sin. Past. Present. Future. We are forgiven in Christ.

=== Summary
# from 16360, 8660, 8690, 10791, 10790, 14934
--- The blood atonement
kicker: Summary
point: The only propitiation | Only the blood of a holy God offered in our place can atone for our sin and justify us before God.
point: Not our works | None of these things satisfy the price of sin.
point: Offered once | Christ was offered once to bear our sins.
point: Perfected for ever | Forgiven of all sin by this perfect sanctification, total remission, forever.
point: While we were yet sinners | God loved His enemies, and offered the free gift of salvation by the shedding of blood of His only begotten Son.
point: Peace with God | We are now reconciled, having made peace with the Father through the blood of the Son.

